Noun ＋ の ＋ とおり（に）') AND c.Explanation COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'とおり(に) says an action happens exactly the way something else describes or predicts. After a verb it uses the plain form — 私が言ったとおりになった = it turned out just as I said; 書いてあるとおりに作る = make it just as it is written. After a noun, join with の — 地図のとおりに行く = go exactly as the map shows. The に is often dropped with no change in meaning.' AND DATALENGTH(c.Explanation) = DATALENGTH(N'とおり(に) says an action happens exactly the way something else describes or predicts. After a verb it uses the plain form — 私が言ったとおりになった = it turned out just as I said; 書いてあるとおりに作る = make it just as it is written. After a noun, join with の — 地図のとおりに行く = go exactly as the map shows. The に is often dropped with no change in meaning.') AND c.UsageNotes COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'After a noun you need の: 地図のとおり, not 地図とおり.
