Verb［dictionary form］＋ と共に') AND c.Explanation COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'と共に has two related uses. With a noun it means ''together with'' — 家族と共に新年を迎えた = I welcomed the new year together with my family. With a verb of change it means ''as ~ happens, so does ...'' — 年を取ると共に体力が落ちる = as you age, your stamina declines. It is a formal, written-flavoured equivalent of 〜と一緒に and 〜につれて.' AND DATALENGTH(c.Explanation) = DATALENGTH(N'と共に has two related uses. With a noun it means ''together with'' — 家族と共に新年を迎えた = I welcomed the new year together with my family. With a verb of change it means ''as ~ happens, so does ...'' — 年を取ると共に体力が落ちる = as you age, your stamina declines. It is a formal, written-flavoured equivalent of 〜と一緒に and 〜につれて.') AND c.UsageNotes COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'It is stiff and written; in casual speech 〜と一緒に is more natural for ''together with''.
