FROM Grammars c WHERE c.Id = @Id AND c.Meaning COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'to; for; from the standpoint of ~' AND DATALENGTH(c.Meaning) = DATALENGTH(N'to; for; from the standpoint of ~') AND c.Formation COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'Noun ＋ にとって（は／も／の）' AND DATALENGTH(c.Formation) = DATALENGTH(N'Noun ＋ にとって（は／も／の）') AND c.Explanation COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'にとって attaches to a noun — usually a person, group, or organization — and weighs something from that party''s standpoint: how it looks, matters, or feels to them. 私にとって = for me / as far as I''m concerned. It is almost always followed by an evaluation (大切だ, 難しい, 幸せだ). Use it to say who something is significant, hard, or valuable for.' AND DATALENGTH(c.Explanation) = DATALENGTH(N'にとって attaches to a noun — usually a person, group, or organization — and weighs something from that party''s standpoint: how it looks, matters, or feels to them. 私にとって = for me / as far as I''m concerned. It is almost always followed by an evaluation (大切だ, 難しい, 幸せだ). Use it to say who something is significant, hard, or valuable for.') AND c.UsageNotes COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'にとって marks whose viewpoint you are judging from; it is not the ''for whose benefit'' に of あげる/くれる. For ''I bought it for my mother'', use のために, not にとって.
Follow it with an evaluation or judgment (大切, 必要, つらい…), not an ordinary action — にとって does not mark the doer of a plain verb.' AND DATALENGTH(c.UsageNotes) = DATALENGTH(N'にとって marks whose viewpoint you are judging from; it is not the ''for whose benefit'' に of あげる/くれる. For ''I bought it for my mother'', use のために, not にとって.
Follow it with an evaluation or judgment (大切, 必要, つらい…), not an ordinary action — にとって does not mark the doer of a plain verb.');
