Verb［dictionary form］＋ ごとに' AND DATALENGTH(c.Formation) = DATALENGTH(N'Noun／counter ＋ ごとに
Verb［dictionary form］＋ ごとに') AND c.Explanation COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'ごとに means ''every'' or ''each'', attaching to a counter, a noun, or a dictionary-form verb. With a counter it marks a regular interval — 四年ごとに = every four years. With a verb it means ''each time...'': 会うごとに = every time we meet. It picks out a repeating unit and says something holds for each one.' AND DATALENGTH(c.Explanation) = DATALENGTH(N'ごとに means ''every'' or ''each'', attaching to a counter, a noun, or a dictionary-form verb. With a counter it marks a regular interval — 四年ごとに = every four years. With a verb it means ''each time...'': 会うごとに = every time we meet. It picks out a repeating unit and says something holds for each one.') AND c.UsageNotes COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'三日ごとに means ''every three days'' (a regular interval). Don''t confuse it with 三日おきに, which leaves three-day gaps (every fourth day).
ごとに attaches freely to counters and verbs; まい (毎〜) instead prefixes set time-words like 毎日, 毎週.' AND DATALENGTH(c.UsageNotes) = DATALENGTH(N'三日ごとに means ''every three days'' (a regular interval). Don''t confuse it with 三日おきに, which leaves three-day gaps (every fourth day).
