With intransitive verbs the actor is usually を (子どもを帰らせる); with transitive verbs the actor takes に, because を is already used by the object (妹に部屋をそうじさせる).' AND DATALENGTH(c.UsageNotes) = DATALENGTH(N'Whether it means ''make'' or ''let'' comes from context, not the form — 休ませる can be forcing a rest or granting one.
