らしくない／らしかった［conjugates like an い-adjective］') AND c.Explanation COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'This らしい is a suffix saying something has the ideal qualities of what it attaches to — 男らしい (''manly''), 子どもらしい (''fittingly childlike''), 春らしい (''spring-like''). It is praise for being a good, typical example of its kind, and it behaves like an い-adjective.' AND DATALENGTH(c.Explanation) = DATALENGTH(N'This らしい is a suffix saying something has the ideal qualities of what it attaches to — 男らしい (''manly''), 子どもらしい (''fittingly childlike''), 春らしい (''spring-like''). It is praise for being a good, typical example of its kind, and it behaves like an い-adjective.') AND c.UsageNotes COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'Positive nuance: 学生らしい means ''admirably student-like'', not merely ''resembles a student'' (which would be 学生のよう).
