な-adjective／Noun ＋ な ＋ んだけど／んですが') AND c.Explanation COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'This joins the explanatory んだ／んです with けど／が (''but''). It sets up background — ''the thing is…'' — and then trails off into a request, question, or contrast. Often the ''but'' is not really adversative; it just softens the approach: すみません、道に迷ったんですが… (''Excuse me, I''ve gotten lost, and…''). んですが is polite, んだけど casual.' AND DATALENGTH(c.Explanation) = DATALENGTH(N'This joins the explanatory んだ／んです with けど／が (''but''). It sets up background — ''the thing is…'' — and then trails off into a request, question, or contrast. Often the ''but'' is not really adversative; it just softens the approach: すみません、道に迷ったんですが… (''Excuse me, I''ve gotten lost, and…''). んですが is polite, んだけど casual.') AND c.UsageNotes COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'Nouns and な-adjectives need な before ん: 学生なんですが, not 学生だんですが.
