何 ＋ も ＋ Verb［negative］') AND c.Explanation COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'Builds indefinite expressions from 何 (what): 何か means "something / anything", while 何も plus a negative verb means "nothing / not anything". The particle decides the meaning — か opens up an unspecified possibility, も with a negative rules everything out.' AND DATALENGTH(c.Explanation) = DATALENGTH(N'Builds indefinite expressions from 何 (what): 何か means "something / anything", while 何も plus a negative verb means "nothing / not anything". The particle decides the meaning — か opens up an unspecified possibility, も with a negative rules everything out.') AND c.UsageNotes COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 = N'何も must pair with a negative verb — 何もない (there''s nothing), not 何もある.
何か is always the indefinite ''something/anything'' — to ask directly ''what is it?'', use 何ですか or 何が~ instead, not 何か alone.' AND DATALENGTH(c.UsageNotes) = DATALENGTH(N'何も must pair with a negative verb — 何もない (there''s nothing), not 何もある.
何か is always the indefinite ''something/anything'' — to ask directly ''what is it?'', use 何ですか or 何が~ instead, not 何か alone.');
